# Applied to EVERY `mvn` invocation run from the repo root (local + CI).
#
# Maven Central occasionally returns HTTP 429 (Too Many Requests) — it rate-limits
# CI runners. Maven Resolver's HTTP retry handler already retries 429/503, but its
# defaults (3 tries, 5s) aren't enough under sustained throttling and a build fails
# with "Could not transfer artifact … status code: 429". Bump the retry budget and
# backoff so transient throttling self-heals instead of red-failing a deploy.
-Daether.connector.http.retryHandler.count=8
-Daether.connector.http.retryHandler.interval=6000
-Daether.connector.http.retryHandler.intervalMax=90000
-Daether.connector.http.retryHandler.serviceUnavailable=429,502,503,504
